 ## Position and ownership
 
-One docking surface exists per Session, held in a session-scoped slot store and drawn by `rightbar.session`. The root-scoped `rightbar` controller retains separate seats for the selected Session and background Sessions with initialized `keepMounted` bodies; only the foreground Conversation is visible. Reload restores saved layouts ([state](../../packages/client/ui-sidebar-right/README.md#state)). The surface's every change is one recorded history entry computed by the kit's pure planners; a docked pane never stays empty, and an empty root pane receives the default page selected from registered guide entries.
+One docking surface exists per Session, held in a session-scoped slot store and drawn by `rightbar.session`. The root-scoped `rightbar` controller retains separate seats for the selected Session and background Sessions with initialized `keepMounted` bodies or rendering holds; only the foreground Conversation is interactive. `ctx.sidebarRight.holdRendering(sessionId)` returns an idempotent release and keeps a background sidebar rendered inert behind the application without selecting it ([rendering holds](../../packages/client/ui-sidebar-right/README.md#ctxsidebarright)). Reload restores saved layouts ([state](../../packages/client/ui-sidebar-right/README.md#state)). The surface's every change is one recorded history entry computed by the kit's pure planners; a docked pane never stays empty, and an empty root pane receives the default page selected from registered guide entries.
 
 A tab type is two registrations that share the definition's `id`: a static definition in `ctx.sidebarRightTabs` saying which addresses its `kind` opens, and a keyed slot registration supplying its body. The framework injects `useTabInfo()` for live Sidebar, pane and tab information; each type keeps its own state in its slot store. Packages import each other's declarations only as types.
 
